1.  You can describe something with words.
	And you can describe something similar
	by manipulating the same sentence.
	
	Now try that with mathematical symbols instead of
	words. By modifying equations that describe real
	actions, you get a new description of a new
	(surprising) action that is likely legitimate.
	
	But you need not start with real-world equations.
	What's merely legitimate in mathematics can be
	modified then applied to the real world.
	
	Suddenly, things like quantum mechanics feels
	like common sense. When AI gains the ability to
	adjust abstraction between prompt and mathematical
	proof, sand daddy is born, and this is how.
